    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_3d4881c52d56e5d01499f01ccaa5babcfbe550bab8a8d79a1a6f8c1ae87ebe46",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "After damping and Fourier transformation, completed L-values become a Dirichlet-coefficient sum against translates of one Mellin kernel G fixed by the damping and archimedean gamma parameters. Contour-residue recurrence and certified local Taylor jets turn that costly kernel into reusable finite data, while a second convolution evaluates all translated coefficient sums together. Explicit Dirichlet-tail and both Poisson-periodization alias bounds then promote the amortized FFT representation from a speedup to a rigorous many-value evaluator for L-functions sharing the same archimedean factor.",
